1a8f1d981f430c\",\"cmd-31f4187bb5ec48c1\",\"cmd-8e1a1f77e1874868\",\"cmd-0d85b536d66140e7\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor correctly and thoroughly implemented the password policy on node1: minlen=12 and minclass=3 in pwquality.conf, with the non-obvious fix of zeroing all four length-credit knobs so the 12-character floor cannot be reduced by extra character classes. Enforcement was verified end-to-end via real passwd changes against boundary cases (short, insufficient-class, and compliant passwords) both before and after a full, well-evidenced node restart that shows the correct boot-identity transition and post-restart recovery of both config and functional enforcement. Operational hygiene is high, with only a superseded intermediate config edit and a retained backup file as minor, low-risk artifacts.\",\"limitations\":[\"Package-health check was unavailable (timed out) both before and after the executor's work, so package-manager consistency around libpwquality could not be independently confirmed, though this did not affect the task's functional verification.\",\"No lifecycle diff evidence exists between before_prepare and after_prepare since prepare was disabled and after_prepare is an alias of before_prepare; all state comparison relies on before_prepare vs after_executor.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"minlen-12","requirement":"New user passwords must be at least 12 characters long on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"pwquality.conf set minlen=12 with all four credit values (dcredit/ucredit/lcredit/ocredit) zeroed so length credits from character classes cannot reduce the effective minimum. Verified via pwscore and real passwd changes that an 11-character password is rejected ('password is shorter than 12 characters') while a 12-character password is accepted, both pre- and post-restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-93a9bdf02aeb4c47","cmd-e208afdd9600429f","cmd-81dbdbe2757a4164","cmd-8e1a1